🎤 Interview Explanation (Short & Perfect)

👉
“I first check if the total sum is even. Then I convert the problem into subset sum with target = sum/2. I use recursion with memoization where at each index I decide to include or exclude the element. The DP state is (index, currentSum), and time complexity is O(n * target).”

🔁 Counter Interview Questions
❓ Q1: Why check sum % 2 != 0?

👉 Odd sum cannot be divided into two equal integer parts

❓ Q2: Why only sum/2?

👉 Because:

subset1 = S/2 → subset2 automatically = S/2
❓ Q3: Why DP?

👉 To avoid recomputation of same (index, sum) states

❓ Q4: Can we optimize space?

👉 Yes → use 1D DP array (boolean[target+1])

❓ Q5: What if negative numbers allowed?

👉 This approach fails ❌
Need different technique (offset / hashmap)

🔥 Common Mistakes (you almost did)

❌ count == sum - count
❌ not checking odd sum
❌ wrong DP state

🧠 Final Memory Trick

